# TypeScript is the source; the .js is committed build output

Files prefixed `~` are TypeScript. **Edit the `.ts`** — the adjacent `.js` and `.js.map` are generated by
the MSBuild TypeScript task and committed, so never hand-edit them and expect the change to survive.

Two registrations are required or the code silently does not exist at runtime:

1. Every new `.ts` needs `<TypeScriptCompile Include="Portals\app\..." />` in `UI/TRiZHub/TRiZHub.csproj`.
2. Every new **service folder** needs its own line in `App_Start/BundleConfig.cs`:
   `.IncludeDirectory("~/Portals/app/services/<X>Service", "*.js")`. There is no wildcard.

State controllers are exempt from bundling — ocLazyLoad fetches them by literal path.

# Services

Extend `CHServiceBase`, call `super(ENV.serverLocation + "api/<X>/")`, and expose one method per WebAPI
action using the `$q.defer()` pattern, rejecting with `error.data.message`. Register with
`angular.module("AngularApp").factory("<X>Service", ["$http", "$q", "ENV", getInstance])`.

# State controllers

Extend `CHControllerBase`, use `const me = this;` and arrow properties so `this` survives callbacks, and
surface failures through `me.handleError(error)` or `me.Popups.showError(me.$scope, error)`. Register with
an explicit DI string array — there is no `$inject` annotation pass, and minification is disabled
(`BundleTable.EnableOptimizations = false`).

Grids are driven by `new TcrGridServiceModule.TcrGridService(defaultSortKey, serviceGridFn, onDataLoaded,
paramMapper, null, $state)`, where `paramMapper` copies filter state onto the request model.

# Routing

Add states to the single `.config` block in `Portals/app/AngularApp.js`, following the existing
abstract-parent plus `grid`/`detail/:id` child pattern, and lazy-load the controller in `resolve`. URLs are
hash-based (`html5Mode(false)`). Note that the `.run` block currently redirects every entry path to
`root.login`.
